<section class="intro section"><div class="wrap content-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow dark">Why we exist</p><h2>Helping property owners move from concern to a plan</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Discovering mold can be stressful. Photographs online often make every dark mark look like an emergency, while quick surface cleaning advice can minimize a genuine moisture problem. Our approach is to slow the situation down enough to understand the building, the water history and the affected materials.</p><p>We serve West Vancouver homeowners, condo owners, strata representatives, tenants, commercial occupants and property managers. The purpose of an assessment is to document what is visible, explain important limitations and identify which next steps are reasonable for the property.</p><p>We do not identify mold species by colour, promise that a building is completely mold free or use fear to create unnecessary work. Testing is recommended when it is likely to answer a specific question. Remediation planning begins with moisture control because cleaning without source correction can allow the same condition to return.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="process-section section"><div class="wrap process-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h2>A straightforward standard</h2><p>Good property decisions come from useful evidence, careful scope and honest communication about what can and cannot be concluded.</p></div><ol class="steps"><li><span>1</span><div><h3>Listen first</h3><p>The history of leaks, odours, repairs and seasonal changes helps direct the investigation.</p></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><h3>Follow the evidence</h3><p>Visible conditions, moisture patterns and building details are considered together.</p></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><h3>Explain limitations</h3><p>Inaccessible areas and unanswered questions are documented rather than hidden behind certainty.</p></div></li><li><span>4</span><div><h3>Prioritize next steps</h3><p>Source correction, further investigation, remediation and repair are placed in a practical order.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap content-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow dark">Local understanding</p><h2>Why West Vancouver buildings need context</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>West Vancouver includes older homes, renovated hillside properties, modern custom construction, waterfront residences, concrete towers and low rise strata buildings. Rain exposure, roof complexity, drainage, shaded sites and indoor humidity affect these properties in different ways.</p><p>A recommendation that makes sense for a small condo window corner may be completely unsuitable for a widespread attic or crawl space condition. Our pages explain those differences so property owners can recognize why the inspection and work plan must match the building.</p><p>If you are unsure which service applies, call <a href="tel:+16048003900">(604) 800-3900</a> or use the form above. Describe what you are seeing, where it is located and whether there has been a leak or water event.</p></div></div></section>
